    "created_at": "2021-04-21T11:13:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-21T11:13:44Z",
    "body": "My gut feeling here would be that what's exposed to/announced by AT should match the visible counter (e.g. if the author set it to roman numerals or whatever, AT should really announce it that way)\r\n\r\noddly though, i'd also be in favour for exposing/announcing regular ordinal value in cases where the author has somehow suppressed the display altogether (there's an ongoing discussion around VoiceOver not announcing lists when they're not styled visually as lists anymore, and there are pros and cons on this approach), so while inconsistent as a position, wonder if it's possible to special case this situation?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
