    "body": "> My gut feeling here would be that what's exposed to/announced by AT should match the visible counter (e.g. if the author set it to roman numerals or whatever,\r\nAT should really announce it that way)\r\n\r\nAgreed. If it were otherwise it would make it next to impossible to give other people meaningful references to the content. Also, adding to @aardrian's point, in certain cases not being able to correctly identify clauses or terms can have legal implications.",
